error[MR0204]: `<<` cannot shift a `double`
 --> tests/ui/types/operators.mr:6:13
  |
6 |     let e = x << 1; //~ ERROR MR0204
  |             -^^^^^
  |             |
  |             this is `double`
  |
  = note: only a value of an integer type can be shifted

error[MR0204]: `!` is not defined for `int`
 --> tests/ui/types/operators.mr:7:13
  |
7 |     let f = !n; //~ ERROR MR0204
  |             ^^ the operand is `int`
  |
  = note: `!` negates a `bool`; compare a number explicitly, as in `x == 0`

error[MR0204]: `+` is not defined for `string` and `int`
 --> tests/ui/types/operators.mr:8:13
  |
8 |     let g = s + n; //~ ERROR MR0204
  |             -^^^-
  |             |   |
  |             |   this is `int`
  |             this is `string`
  |
  = note: `+` joins two `string` values; interpolation formats other values as text, as in `$"{a}{b}"`

